    "sourceWikitext": "{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Korean recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} \n\n'''Korean shortribs''' or '''bulgogi''' is a kind of Korean barbecue, using shortribs that have been marinated in soy sauce, scallion, ginger, chiles, garlic, and sesame oil. The marinated meat is then slow-grilled or baked.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* ⅓ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Green Onion|scallions]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 6 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], smashed and [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 1 ½ [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] toasted [[Cookbook:Sesame Oil|sesame oil]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] fresh [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Canola Oil|canola oil]]\n* 4 Thai bird [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]], stemmed\n* 12 English-cut [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]] shortribs\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Process all ingredients except meat in a [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]] until smooth. Pour into a gallon size zip-top bag, and add shortribs.\n#[[Cookbook:Mixing#Tossing|Toss]] to coat the meat in the marinade, and refrigerate overnight. Note that this flavors but does not tenderize the meat.\n#Preheat grill to 225–300°F. Add shortribs and cover. Cook 5 hours or until meat falls right off the bone and is extremely tender. Serve immediately.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using beef rib]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bird chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Barbecue recipes]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Korean recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]",
